# Surface Pro 12 (Intel): the front camera relay with automatic framing
# (sp12-autoframe). Loaded after sp12-front.conf by the relay unit drop-in,
# so this VIDEOSRC replaces that one. Not a .conf: v4l2-relayd's generator
# starts one relay per *.conf in this directory. `sp12-autoframe off` shows the whole
# field of view; settings live in /run/sp12/autoframe.
#
# Two pipelines, pick one (restart v4l2-relayd@sp12-front after a change):
#
# Crop mode (default): 3840x2160 from the ISP, the element crops and scales on
# the CPU. About 25 % of a core with the camera open. The ISP's temporal noise
# reduction is fully effective at 4K, so this is the cleaner picture.
VIDEOSRC="icamerasrc device-name=imx681-uf fps-range=15~30 ! video/x-raw,format=NV12,width=3840,height=2160,framerate=30/1 ! sp12autoframe model=/usr/share/sp12/face_detection_yunet_2023mar.onnx control-file=/run/sp12/autoframe ! video/x-raw,format=NV12,width=1920,height=1080 ! videoconvert"
#
# ISP mode: 1080p from the ISP, the element only detects and sends the window
# upstream as icamerasrc's zoom-region; the ISP crops and scales (needs
# sp12-camera-hal 2025.12.10-4 or later). About 17 % of a core, but the ISP's
# temporal noise reduction is much weaker in its 1080p configuration, so the
# picture is noisier, most visibly when zoomed in (docs/auto-framing-plan.md).
#VIDEOSRC="icamerasrc device-name=imx681-uf fps-range=15~30 ! video/x-raw,format=NV12,width=1920,height=1080,framerate=30/1 ! sp12autoframe mode=isp model=/usr/share/sp12/face_detection_yunet_2023mar.onnx control-file=/run/sp12/autoframe ! video/x-raw,format=NV12,width=1920,height=1080 ! videoconvert"
